{"kind":"assistant","seq":18,"at":"2026-10-14T10:43:58.056Z","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pressing P now toggles pause in the GameScene. While paused, the player is frozen and \"PAUSED\" shows in the middle of the screen. The two unit tests pass. I haven't run the game in a browser, so the key handling and the overlay are untested.\n\n- **Pause flag:** `src/logic/score.js` now has `paused: false` in `createState` and a new `togglePause(state)` that flips it and leaves the other fields alone.\n- **Test:** `test/score.test.js` checks that the flag toggles on and off and that `coins` is unchanged.\n- **Scene:** `src/scenes/GameScene.js` adds a hidden \"PAUSED\" text at (400, 300). A `keydown-P` handler toggles the state, shows or hides the text, and calls `physics.pause()` or `physics.resume()`. `update()` returns early while paused, so held arrow keys don't move the player.\n\nI pause the physics world as well as skipping `update()`, so anything else with velocity also stops.","citations":null}],"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"input":2,"cacheRead":9426,"cacheWrite":1375,"output":327},"costUsd":0.0106592,"latencyMs":3152,"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptParts":[["tools",4016],["system",1900],["user",385],["prompt",42],["assistant",18],["toolResults",78],["assistant",65],["files",562],["assistant",558],["toolResults",220]],"snapshot":"011352c210ee71eb1c0df44d9a74e487","timing":{"startAt":1791974634852,"requestAt":1791974634899,"firstTokenAt":1791974638041,"firstAnswerAt":1791974638041,"lastTokenAt":1791974638050,"endAt":1791974638056}}
